export anchor PeriodicTableStyle:
    number: 127
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Periodic table
    idea: Every number and project becomes an element tile with a number, a two-letter symbol and a mass, arranged in the classic table shape with the greeting in the gap and the chart and activity as detached series rows below.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #fafaf7, the page
        ink: #1a1a1a, text, 1.5px tile borders, the primary button and the current nav cell
        muted: #4d4d4d, masses, meta and captions
        summary: #e3e0f3, the four number tiles
        design: #ffd8b0, design family tiles
        engineering: #c7dcf7, engineering family tiles
        research: #cdeccd, research family tiles
        marketing: #f3cde6, marketing family tiles
        alarm: #f9c8c3, the overdue tile and alert
        lastWeekFill: #a9c46b, day tile fill on #eef2e2 for last week
        thisWeekFill: #7fb0e8, day tile fill on #eaf1fa for this week
        onTrack: #17663a, the filled circle
        atRisk: #8a4b00, the filled triangle
        behind: #a3201a, the heavy cross
        focus: #5b3fd1, the 3px focus outline
    type:
        Symbols and values use Helvetica Neue, Arial Black, Arial, sans-serif
        at 800. Text uses Avenir Next, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Arial,
        sans-serif. The greeting is 40px 700 at 1.1, symbols 40 to 44px,
        values 32px, names 14px 700, body 15px at 1.45, meta and atomic
        numbers 12px, series labels 13px caps.
    layout:
        A header with a Bw element tile as the logo, the brand with the line
        The periodic table of your week, then a square search, a black New
        project button, a square bell and an Mo tile avatar. The nav is a
        row of six ruled cells numbered 1 to 6, Home filled black. The main
        table is an eight column grid with 6px gutters. Rows one and two hold
        the number tiles at the far left and right, Ap 6, Dw 23, Ot 4 in the
        alarm colour and Hl 186, with the greeting, date and an alert chip
        for 4 tasks are overdue filling the gap between them on faint ruled
        lines. Row three holds the six project tiles numbered 7 to 12, each
        in its team colour with the percent as mass in the top right, a big
        symbol such as Wr or Bm, the name, team, tasks and due date, a thin
        black progress bar and a white bordered status chip. A dashed Key
        tile explains the tile anatomy and the colour families. Below, two
        series rows with a thick rule label on the left. The chart is
        fourteen day tiles filled from the bottom to each value, green for
        last week and blue for this week, with week totals under them.
        Reactions shows activity as tiles with an initials symbol. Below
        1000px the table becomes four columns with the greeting on top and
        projects two per row, and day tiles wrap to two rows of seven.
    spacing: 6px gutters between tiles like a printed chart, 8px tile padding and 28px between the table and each series row.
    density: A dense grid of equal cells. Eight columns wide, four below 1000px.
    corners: Square on every tile, field and button.
    borders: 1.5px ink round every cell, dashed for the key, a 3px rule above series labels.
    shadows: None. Colour families and borders do all the grouping.
    icons:
        Tiny solid status glyphs at 14px in a white chip with the word, a
        filled circle for On track, a filled triangle for At risk and a
        heavy cross for Behind. Two-letter symbols stand in for icons
        elsewhere.
    focus: A 3px violet outline offset 2px.
    tone: Chemistry class labels such as Key, Reactions and The periodic table of your week, plain values otherwise.
